    "introduction": "This guide will be showing you how to remove and replace the thread cutter on a Brother CS6000i sewing machine. The thread cutter is a handy feature that allows the user to safely and easily cut the excess thread from the machine and workpiece. Some symptoms related to a faulty thread cutter are the thread not cutting when attempting to use the cutter (dull blade) or the thread cutter being overly exposed and no longer safe due to a broken blade enclosure.",
    "what_you_need": {
        "tools": [
            {
                "text": "Phillips #2 Screwdriver",
                "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/products/6-in-1-screwdriver",
                "image": "https://cart-products.cdn.ifixit.com/cart-products/LYcK13TjejldWD5Y.thumbnail",
                "price": "$6.99"
            }
        ]
    },
    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Thread Cutter",
            "text": "Take off the the white cover on the front left side.",
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/CYCdZlVNwIRnll64.medium",
            "image_links": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/CYCdZlVNwIRnll64.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/Xn43wdTf5seGaNZM.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/179939/384299",
            "comment_links": [],
            "additional_images": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/Xn43wdTf5seGaNZM.medium"
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Remove the 8 mm Phillips #2 screw securing the thread cutter to the housing.",
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/ksaUFcCrroVQfpou.medium",
            "image_links": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/ksaUFcCrroVQfpou.200x150",
